<!-- Settings, at the weight of the row it lives in.

     Same drawing as the traced original - rows at y 29.5 / 47.5 / 65.5, knobs
     centred at x 61.5 / 33.5 / 57.5 - carrying a heavier stroke: bars 8 units
     rather than 6, knobs radius 7 rather than 6.

     That is not a taste call. Rendered and counted, the 6-unit version put
     252 dp-squared of ink on screen against the reload ring's 339, so it was
     the one thin thing in a row with a bold wordmark and a solid mark in it.
     8 and 7 land on 342, which is 1.01x the ring.

     The two short stubs are widened to the stroke width. A segment narrower
     than its own stroke has no straight part left, and the rounded-rect path
     below would cross its own ends over and invert. -->
